{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35381","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Monosaccharid","Monosaccharide","Monosacharid","monosacarido","monosacaridos","monosaccharides"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_35381","description":["Parent monosaccharides are polyhydroxy aldehydes H[CH(OH)]\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cem\u003en\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003eC(\u003dO)H or polyhydroxy ketones H‒[CHOH]\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cem\u003en\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e‒C(\u003dO)[CHOH]\u003csmall\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cem\u003em\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/small\u003e‒H with three or more carbon atoms. The generic term \u0027monosaccharide\u0027 (as opposed to oligosaccharide or polysaccharide) denotes a single unit, without glycosidic connection to other such units. It includes aldoses, dialdoses, aldoketoses, ketoses and diketoses, as well as deoxy sugars, provided that the parent compound has a (potential) carbonyl group."],"label":"monosaccharide","obo_id":"CHEBI:35381","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["monosaccharides"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_140358","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["a monosaccharide 1-phosphate","monosaccharide 1-monophosphate(2-)","sugar 1-monophosphate(2-)"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_140358","description":["An organophosphate oxoanion obtained by deprotonation of the phosphate OH groups of any monosaccharide 1-phosphate.This compound class represents generic and unspecified sugar 1-phosphates."],"label":"monosaccharide 1-phosphate(2-)","obo_id":"CHEBI:140358","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_140359","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["UDP-sugar(2-)","a UDP-monosaccharide"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_140359","description":["A nucleotide-sugar oxoanion obtained by deprotonation of the phosphate OH groups of any UDP-monosaccharide. This compound class represents generic and unspecified UDP-sugars."],"label":"UDP-monosaccharide(2-)","obo_id":"CHEBI:140359","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24589","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["monosaccharide sulfates"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_24589","description":["Any carbohydrate sulfate that is a monosaccharide carrying at least one \u003cem\u003eO\u003c/em\u003e-sulfo substituent."],"label":"monosaccharide sulfate","obo_id":"CHEBI:24589","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_60926","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["amino monosaccharides"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_60926","description":["Any  amino sugar that is a monosaccharide in which one alcoholic hydroxy group is replaced by an amino group."],"label":"amino monosaccharide","obo_id":"CHEBI:60926","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63367","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["monosaccharide derivatives"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_63367","description":["A carbohydrate derivative that is formally obtained from a monosaccharide."],"label":"monosaccharide derivative","obo_id":"CHEBI:63367","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_78848","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["monosaccharide residues"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_78848","description":["The divalent organic group that is one constituent monosaccharide unit of an oligo- or poly-saccharide, formed by loss the anomeric hydroxy group and of H from one of the remaining hydroxy groups."],"label":"monosaccharide residue","obo_id":"CHEBI:78848","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_29524","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Avermectin A1a monosaccharide"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_29524","description":[],"label":"Avermectin A1a monosaccharide","obo_id":"CHEBI:29524","type":"class"},